<sst uniqueCount="793" xmlns="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/spreadsheetml/2006/main"><si><t>Architecture</t></si><si><t>AI Entity</t></si><si><t>Input/Output Files</t></si><si><t>Creation Method</t></si><si><t>Data Hub</t></si><si><t>Source Files/Data/Documents</t></si><si><t>Offer Architecture PPTs/Presentations</t></si><si><t>Core Files</t></si><si><t>Manual</t></si><si><t>Generated</t></si><si><t>Log and Versioning</t></si><si><t>ChatBots</t></si><si><t>Purpose</t></si><si><t>Use Cases</t></si><si><t>Agents</t></si><si><t>Inputs</t></si><si><t>Outputs</t></si><si><t>Business Processes</t></si><si><t>Story</t></si><si><t>Story 1:</t></si><si><t>Joe Montana:  I was the Mailman for my Guys</t></si><si><t>US Postal &quot;unofficial&quot; Creed</t></si><si><t>“Neither snow nor rain nor heat nor gloom of night stays these couriers from the swift completion of their appointed rounds.”</t></si><si><t>Added;  Anthrax</t></si><si><t>20th Anniversary of 9/11/2001 Anthrax Mailings</t></si><si><t>Mission Statement</t></si><si><t>&quot;Provide postal services to bind the Nation together through the personal, educational, literary, and business correspondence of the people.&quot;</t></si><si><t>The text is carved into the main facade of the James A. Farley Post Office in New York City.</t></si><si><t>Story 2:</t></si><si><t>AI-Vengers</t></si><si><t>1.  Team-up of BU Operations &amp; AI Agents into a Super Team (i.e. JLA, Avengers, Lebron, LOEG)</t></si><si><t>2.  Focus on our AI-Venters End Game.</t></si><si><t>Story 3:</t></si><si><t>Chuck:  Cisco Systems are the &quot;Plumbers of the Internet&quot;</t></si><si><t>We are the Super Mario Brothers</t></si><si><t>Story 4:</t></si><si><t>Pick-up Basketball</t></si><si><t>Can you show me an animation of Sprint Right Option = &quot;The Catch&quot;</t></si><si><t>Story 5:</t></si><si><t>The Bat Signal</t></si><si><t>It is a specially modified searchlight that projects a giant, stylized bat emblem onto the clouds over Gotham City.</t></si><si><t>Typically stationed on the roof of the Gotham City Police Department headquarters,</t></si><si><t>it is most famously used by Commissioner James Gordon to summon Batman during major crises or emergencies</t></si><si><t>The Cry:  Avengers Assemble</t></si><si><t>The phrase was first penned by Stan Lee and made its comic debut in Avengers #10 in 1964</t></si><si><r><rPr><b val="1"/><sz val="12"/><color indexed="8"/><rFont val="Aptos Narrow"/></rPr><t>Rallying Cry:</t></r><r><rPr><sz val="12"/><color indexed="8"/><rFont val="Aptos Narrow"/></rPr><t xml:space="preserve"> Rather than just a literal instruction to stand in formation, it acts as a battle signal</t></r></si><si><t xml:space="preserve">It functions as a rallying cry meant to inspire the heroes, draw them together as a unified force, and focus everyone on the mission at hand </t></si><si><r><rPr><b val="1"/><sz val="12"/><color indexed="8"/><rFont val="Aptos Narrow"/></rPr><t>Symbol of Unity</t></r><r><rPr><sz val="12"/><color indexed="8"/><rFont val="Aptos Narrow"/></rPr><t xml:space="preserve">: The phrase embodies the core spirit of the Avengers: putting aside personal differences, </t></r></si><si><t>trusting one another, and standing united to defend the world against threats too big to handle alone.</t></si><si><t>Story 6:</t></si><si><t>Sneaker Test</t></si><si><t>The Entrepreneurial &quot;Sneaker Test&quot;</t></si><si><t>What it means: It suggests that founders who wear dirty, scuffed white sneakers are often more focused on building their companies than on maintaining a polished, appearance-conscious look. It is used as a shorthand for spotting a &quot;real builder.&quot;</t></si><si><t>The Footwear &quot;Sneaker Test&quot;</t></si><si><t>When shopping for shoes, a &quot;sneaker test&quot; refers to a quick quality and fit evaluation to ensure comfort and support.</t></si><si><t>Squeeze &amp; Flex Test: You press the toe box and bend the shoe. It should flex at the toe but remain firm in the middle to properly support your foot arch.</t></si><si><t>Heel Hug Test: Walking around to ensure your heel doesn't slip out, which can cause blisters.</t></si><si><t>Story 7:</t></si><si><t>Bill Walsh</t></si><si><t>What was Bill Walsh's famous quote?</t></si><si><t xml:space="preserve">Bill Walsh's most famous leadership philosophy and mantra is: &quot;The score takes care of itself.&quot; He detailed this process-driven mindset in his renowned leadership book, The Score Takes Care of Itself. </t></si><si><t xml:space="preserve">He also famously believed in focusing on actions rather than the prize, advising, &quot;Concentrate on what will produce results rather than on the results, the process rather than the prize.&quot; </t></si><si><t>San Francisco 49ers Coach Bill Walsh and QB Joe Montana, 1985 NFC Championship</t></si><si><t>JANUARY 06: Football: NFC Playoffs, San Francisco 49ers coach Bill Walsh with QB Joe Montana (16) during game vs Chicago Bears, San Francisco, CA 1/6/1985 (Photo by Michael Zagaris/Sports Illustrated via Getty Images/Getty Images) (SetNumber: D83275)</t></si><si><t>BU Operations: AI Data Hub</t></si><si><t>Legal Documents</t></si><si><t>Master Agreement</t></si><si><t xml:space="preserve">AI:  PID Lifecycle Orchestration </t></si><si><t>Cisco PID Lifecycle Tools/Stakeholders</t></si><si><t>End Results</t></si><si><t>Price Lists</t></si><si><t>Human</t></si><si><t>Agent 0</t></si><si><t>1.  Intake Locker</t></si><si><t>3.  AI Generated Templates</t></si><si><t>Special Quotes/COGS</t></si><si><t>BU Operations</t></si><si><t>AI Data Hub</t></si><si><t>eGenie PID Creation</t></si><si><t>Tools</t></si><si><t>CCW Orderability</t></si><si><t>Team</t></si><si><t>Intake Locker</t></si><si><t>eGenie Price Change</t></si><si><t>eGenie</t></si><si><t>CCW Renewal</t></si><si><t>Manager</t></si><si><t>PID Request Excel</t></si><si><t>Price OPS Pricing Uplift</t></si><si><t>Agent TBD</t></si><si><t>OWB</t></si><si><t xml:space="preserve">CCW 